514	BTN	GGR_NGDP	Bhutan	General government revenue	Revenue consists of taxes, social contributions, grants receivable, and other revenue. Revenue increases government?s net worth, which is the difference between its assets and liabilities (GFSM 2001, paragraph 4.20). Note: Transactions that merely change the composition of the balance sheet do not change the net worth position, for example, proceeds from sales of nonfinancial and financial assets or incurrence of liabilities.	Percent of GDP		See notes for:  General government revenue (National currency).	n/a	48.361	36.478	42.954	43.125	46.967	47.162	48.841	48.612	38.186	29.819	31.584	32.271	41.577	39.313	39.291	42.117	37.403	33.726	40.505	41.284	39.713	36.425	25.615	34.269	30.723	35.038	35.689	35.158	40.431	46.353	35.786	35.796	30.228	33.628	28.942	31.547	27.187	27.278	25.793	32.203	29.071	2014
