544	LAO	GGXWDG	Lao P.D.R.	General government gross debt	Gross debt consists of all liabilities that require payment or payments of interest and/or principal by the debtor to the creditor at a date or dates in the future. This includes debt liabilities in the form of SDRs, currency and deposits, debt securities, loans, insurance, pensions and standardized guarantee schemes, and other accounts payable. Thus, all liabilities in the GFSM 2001 system are debt, except for equity and investment fund shares and financial derivatives and employee stock options. Debt can be valued at current market, nominal, or face values (GFSM 2001, paragraph 7.110).	National currency	Billions	Source: Ministry of Finance or Treasury Latest actual data: 2012/13 Start/end months of reporting year: October/September GFS Manual used: Government Finance Statistics Manual (GFSM) 2001 Basis of recording: Cash General government includes: Central Government Primary domestic currency: Lao kip Data last updated: 08/2016	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	15,799.877	18,779.078	21,331.286	22,641.669	23,790.160	24,601.820	25,272.076	27,020.797	29,848.344	33,182.005	35,294.278	43,747.130	48,221.606	58,434.147	63,431.733	68,040.432	75,718.496	84,606.679	94,892.944	106,000.448	117,728.135	2013
