686	MAR	NGDP_FY	Morocco	Gross domestic product corresponding to fiscal year, current prices	Gross domestic product corresponding to fiscal year is the country?s GDP based on the same period during the year as their fiscal data. In the case of countries whose fiscal data are based on a fiscal calendar (e.g., July to June), this series would be the country?s GDP over that same period. For countries whose fiscal data are based on a calendar year (i.e., January to December), this series will be the same as their GDP in current prices.	National currency	Billions	Source: Ministry of Economy and/or Planning Latest actual data: 2015 Fiscal assumptions: Authorties' and staff estimates Start/end months of reporting year: January/December GFS Manual used: Government Finance Statistics Manual (GFSM) 2001 Basis of recording: Accrual General government includes: Central Government;. Other level fiscal data is not available from the authorities. Valuation of public debt: Face value Primary domestic currency: Moroccan dirham Data last updated: 09/2016	86.600	92.379	108.583	115.883	131.314	151.374	180.851	183.161	212.999	226.677	248.754	281.096	287.825	294.364	327.665	333.319	376.191	372.962	401.524	408.177	412.897	446.012	465.492	498.482	528.764	552.671	603.737	647.532	716.959	748.483	784.624	820.077	847.881	897.923	923.696	982.223	1,017.226	1,071.027	1,126.932	1,196.319	1,271.836	1,354.419	2015
